      "difficulty_level": "H3",
      "difficulty_reason": "The authors regularize arbitrary Gaussian partitions to polynomial threshold partitions, control surface area and rounding while retaining noise stability, then reconstruct low-dimensional polynomial systems through tensor decompositions, multilinearization, mollification and quantitative sign/collision control. The complete local dimension-reduction construction is retained. Original computable (not primitive-recursive) dimension, approximate part-measure preservation and positive-noise parameter are explicit.",
